worktree: ../okay-wt-outbox
spec: specs/outbox.md (new) — BACKLOG "resilience" / microservices-next

why: the microservices audit's largest remaining gap. Queues.ingress/
  egress bridge FOREIGN brokers; when the truth is in our OWN SQL
  database nothing carries a business transaction's event into the
  log atomically (specs/jdbc.md refuses it only for THEIR databases),
  no consumer dedups durably across restarts, and a poison record
  blocks its partition for ever.

what: new module okay-outbox (okay-sql + okay-persist): Outbox (a row
  in the same transaction, a relay into a Topic, at-least-once with
  the outbox id as the record key), Inbox (once-by-id inside the
  consumer's transaction, the unique constraint as the idempotency
  machinery), DeadLetter (a consumer loop that retries, then parks
  the record with its error in a DLQ topic and moves on; replay).
  DDL as values for our own databases. Tests on H2 + MemoryStore.
  Docs: docs/modules/okay-outbox.md, index row, spec.

next: 8 tests green on JVM (H2 + MemoryStore); cross-compile check, commit, gate, land
